@startuml Forgot_Password_System_Sequence_Diagram

title System Sequence Diagram: Forgot Password Function\n(Administrator and Tourist via Email and OTP Verification)

actor "User\n(Tourist/Admin)" as User
participant "UI: Login/Register\nPage" as UI
participant "Email Service\n(Nodemailer)" as Email
participant "Database\n(MongoDB)" as DB
participant "Authentication\nService" as Auth

== Forgot Password Flow ==

User -> UI: Click "Forgot Password"
activate UI

UI -> UI: Display email input

User -> UI: Enter email address

UI -> Email: POST /api/auth/send-otp\n{email}
activate Email

Email -> DB: Check if user exists
activate DB

alt User Not Found
    DB --> Email: User not found
    deactivate DB
    Email --> UI: User not found
    UI --> User: Show error message
else User Exists
    DB -> DB: Generate 6-digit OTP\n(10-minute expiry)
    
    DB --> Email: OTP generated
    deactivate DB
    
    Email -> Email: Send OTP email
    Email --> User: OTP sent via email
    deactivate Email
    
    Email --> UI: OTP sent successfully
    
    UI -> UI: Switch to password reset form\n(start 10-minute countdown)
    
    UI --> User: Display OTP input and\nnew password form
end

deactivate UI

== Reset Password with OTP ==

User -> UI: Enter OTP and new password
activate UI

UI -> UI: Validate password strength\n(min 8 chars, uppercase,\nnumber, special char)

alt Validation Failed
    UI --> User: Show validation errors
else Validation Success
    UI -> Auth: POST /api/auth/reset-password\n{email, otp, newPassword}
    activate Auth
    
    Auth -> DB: Verify OTP and expiry
    activate DB
    
    alt OTP Invalid or Expired
        DB --> Auth: Invalid/Expired OTP
        deactivate DB
        Auth --> UI: Reset failed
        UI --> User: Show error with\nresend option
    else OTP Valid
        DB -> DB: Hash new password
        
        DB -> DB: Update user password\nand clear OTP
        
        DB --> Auth: Password updated
        deactivate DB
        
        Auth --> UI: Password reset successful
        deactivate Auth
        
        UI -> UI: Clear form and\nreturn to login view
        
        UI --> User: Show success message\n"Please log in"
    end
end

deactivate UI

== Resend OTP (Password Reset) ==

User -> UI: Click "Resend OTP"\n(60s cooldown)
activate UI

UI -> Email: POST /api/auth/send-otp\n{email}
activate Email

Email -> DB: Generate new OTP\n(10-minute expiry)
activate DB
DB --> Email: New OTP generated
deactivate DB

Email -> Email: Send new OTP email
Email --> User: New OTP sent
deactivate Email

Email --> UI: OTP resent successfully
UI -> UI: Reset countdown timer\n(60s cooldown)
UI --> User: Show success message

deactivate UI

note right of User
  **Key Features:**
  • OTP expires in 10 minutes
  • Resend cooldown: 60 seconds
  • Password requirements: min 8 chars, 
    1 uppercase, 1 number, 1 special char
  • User must exist in database
  • OTP verified before password update
  • Password hashed before storage
  • Returns to login after successful reset
end note

@enduml
